# Software Development Paradigms Rule

Follow core paradigms and best practices.

## SOLID Principles
- SRP: One reason to change per class/component
- OCP: Open to extend, closed to modify
- LSP: Subtypes must be substitutable
- ISP: No client depends on unused methods
- DIP: Depend on abstractions, not concretions

## React Best Practices
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Keep components single-purpose
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Define clear props interfaces (TypeScript)
- Choose appropriate state management (local/context/store)
- Use React.memo/useMemo/useCallback when appropriate
- Add error boundaries and handling

## Code Organization
- Keep modules small; split into meaningful sub-modules
- Make minimal necessary changes
- Use incremental steps for large changes
- Separate concerns: business vs presentation
- Separate styling from logic
- Use consistent, descriptive naming

## Refactoring
- Identify smallest unit of change
- Propose incremental improvements
- Maintain backward compatibility when possible
- Test each incremental change
- Document architectural decisions

## Avoid Unused Code
- Follow YAGNI: Only implement what you need now
- Throw explicit errors for unsupported cases instead of generic fallbacks
- Use specific names that reflect current capabilities
- Don't add "future-proofing" code without concrete use cases
- Make limitations clear in error messages and comments